1
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:08,790
How does a change really get from my laptop to production?

2
00:00:09,333 --> 00:00:17,692
Everything from the previous modules, in the order a DevOps team uses it every day, on a realistic repository:

3
00:00:17,692 --> 00:00:25,746
an application, a Dockerfile, a Helm chart, Kubernetes manifests, scripts, documentation and CI workflows.

4
00:00:25,746 --> 00:00:30,913
One change goes from a developer's branch all the way to production.

5
00:00:32,667 --> 00:00:39,411
Ada adds chai to the menu, on a branch named by convention, with a Conventional Commit message:

6
00:00:41,167 --> 00:00:41,417
2.

7
00:00:41,417 --> 00:00:44,171
CI locally, then push.

8
00:00:45,933 --> 00:00:49,439
The PR is "merge feat/add-chai into main".

9
00:00:49,439 --> 00:00:59,623
Grace reviews exactly what GitHub would show (lesson 51) and runs the checks on the branch (what ci.yml does on every PR):

10
00:01:01,367 --> 00:01:02,812
Approved and green:

11
00:01:02,812 --> 00:01:08,136
merged with a merge commit (the PR button), and the branch is deleted:

12
00:01:09,900 --> 00:01:14,078
Ada updates main and releases 1.1.0 (a new feature:

13
00:01:14,078 --> 00:01:15,306
minor version).

14
00:01:15,306 --> 00:01:23,989
The script sets the version in VERSION, the chart and the image tag, re-runs the checks, commits and tags:

15
00:01:25,733 --> 00:01:31,193
Production serves four items; the deployed version is exactly the tagged commit.

16
00:01:32,933 --> 00:01:34,649
Let me try something.

17
00:01:34,649 --> 00:01:35,955
The next change:

18
00:01:35,955 --> 00:01:42,653
Ada raises the latte price and, "while she is at it", bumps the image tag by hand.

19
00:01:43,200 --> 00:01:44,816
The PR's CI is red:

20
00:01:44,816 --> 00:01:47,622
image tag matches VERSION failed.

21
00:01:47,622 --> 00:01:53,150
values.yaml now says 1.1.1 while VERSION and the chart say 1.1.0:

22
00:01:53,150 --> 00:01:57,828
the deployment would run an image that was never built.

23
00:01:57,828 --> 00:02:00,889
In review, Grace points at the line:

24
00:02:02,633 --> 00:02:07,682
Ada removes the version change from her commit (her own branch:

25
00:02:07,682 --> 00:02:16,258
amend and force-push with lease, lesson 42), CI goes green, and the PR can be merged and released as 1.1.1:

26
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:20,149
So what is the shape of it?

27
00:02:20,700 --> 00:02:22,101
The DevOps flow:

28
00:02:22,101 --> 00:02:28,669
branch → commit → push → PR → review → CI → merge → release (tag) → deploy.

29
00:02:29,233 --> 00:02:34,443
CI scripts in the repository run the same locally and in GitHub Actions.

30
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:41,739
Versions change only at release; releases are tags; deployment and rollback use tags.
